        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ethics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The move from \"is\" to \"ought\" requires a BRIDGE:\nan additional normative premise."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#009",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ethics:00-overview, git-history:ethics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ethics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Without a bridge: the inference is invalid.\nThe is/ought gap is fundamental to ethics."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#010",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ethics:00-overview, git-history:ethics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ethics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MORAL NATURALISM tries to bridge it:\n\"Suffering is bad\" -- if \"bad\" = \"causes pain\" (a natural property),\nthen natural facts DO entail normative conclusions.\nG.E. Moore's open question argument attacks this (see 01-METAETHICS.md)."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#011",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ethics:00-overview, git-history:ethics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ethics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MORAL NON-NATURALISM: The bridge is a sui generis normative fact.\nMoral facts are not natural facts."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#012",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ethics:00-overview, git-history:ethics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "ethics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ethics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHY IT MATTERS FOR AI:\n  When we derive \"AI should not deceive\" from \"deception causes harm\":\n  we need a bridge (e.g., utilitarianism, deontological rule).\n  Different bridges give different conclusions.\n  AI alignment is fundamentally a normative ethics problem.\n```"
    },
